    <title>Macaulay2 C++ engine documentation</title>
    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The Macaulay2 engine implements rings, elements in these rings, matrices over these rings, mutable matrices, ring maps, and computations including</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Groebner bases</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Hilbert functions</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>free resolutions</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The engine is written in C++ over a long period of time, some of it before the c++ standard library was available or robust. The engine is being updated to c++17, and eventually to c++20.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__rings" kindref="compound">Rings</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__matrices" kindref="compound">Matrices</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__comp" kindref="compound">Computations</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
